hypotheses.statement:
There is an absolute constant $b_0$ with the following property. Let $b\ge b_0$, let $H$ be a finite abelian group written additively, and suppose that $$\log |H|\le b^4,
  \qquad 0\le g\le \exp(b^{0.65}),
  \qquad \bar g:=\mathbb E_{x\in H}g(x)\in[1/2,2].$$ Let $s$ be an integer satisfying $b^{0.69}\le s\le b$, and choose $w_1,\ldots,w_s$ independently and uniformly in $H$. With $c_*=(\log 2)/8$, the probability that $$\label{eq:sampler-conclusion}
  2^{-s}\sum_{\varepsilon\in\{0,1\}^s}
  g\left(x-\sum_{i=1}^s\varepsilon_iw_i\right)
  \ge (1-3b^{-1/10})\bar g
  \qquad\text{for every }x\in H$$ is at least $$\label{eq:sampler-probability}
  1-\exp(-c_*b^{0.69})
    -b\exp\left(-\frac{c_*}{2}b^{0.59}\right).$$ In particular, the failure probability is at most $b^{-1/2}$ after increasing $b_0$.

Let $\mathcal T=\mathbb R^m/\Lambda_h$, and let $U_a\subset\mathcal T$ be measurable sets with $|U_a|\le\eta_a$, where $\eta_a>0$. For $0\le q\le D$, let $\mathcal P_q$ be finite families of labeled patterns in $\mathbb R^q$, binary by suffixes. Suppose they are closed under last-coordinate slicing. Write $$Q=\sum_{q=0}^D|\mathcal P_q|,\qquad L_*>\max(1,Q).$$ There are real vectors $Z_1,\ldots,Z_D\in\mathbb R^m$ such that, for every $P\in\mathcal P_q$, $$\label{eq:shear-bound}
 \left|\bigcap_{l\in P}
   \left(U_{a(l)}+
     \pi_{\Lambda_h}\left(\sum_{j=1}^q l[j]Z_j\right)\right)\right|
 \le L_*^{|P|-1}\prod_{l\in P}\eta_{a(l)}.$$ Here $l[j]$ denotes the $j$th scalar coordinate of $l$.

evidence.quote:
For a convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$, its lattice covering density is $$\theta_L(K)=\inf\left\{
 \frac{\operatorname{vol}_n(K)}{\det\Lambda}:\Lambda\text{ is a full-rank lattice and }
 K+\Lambda=\mathbb R^n\right\}.$$

